      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Ristikontra",
          "subtitle": "Card game",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Ristikontra is a Finnish Sedma-group game for 4 in partnerships. Tricks won by the last card of same rank as led (no suit hierarchy). 6 cards each; stock. Point cards: A=11, 10=10, K=4, Q=3, J=2 (120 total). 61+ points = 1 game point. First to 7 wins. May play top stock 'in the dark'."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Ristikontra is a Finnish game for four players, popular in lumber camps, and is likely the original of the Sedma group. In that group, tricks are won by the last card of equal rank to the card led. These games are played only in a region from Lapland in the north to Hungary in the south; Ristikontra is the Finnish member of that Central European ace–ten family."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "4 in partnerships."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "52 cards. No ranking; suits irrelevant."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deck."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "6 each; rest stock."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Variations",
          "subtitle": "Known ways this game changes",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "style": "unordered",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Ristiklappi: 5 cards; clean rule."
                },
                {
                  "text": "Kontra: 2-3 players, no partnerships."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
